---
title: "check-superset diagnostics"
---

This document deliberately trips every static `taliesin check` superset validator. It
lives in `corpus/diagnostics/`, which is exempt from the corpus clean-render guards.

## Heading {#dup}

First section.

## Another {#dup}

A second heading reusing the same explicit id (duplicate DOM id).

A [broken in-page jump](#no-such-anchor) that lands nowhere, and a missing image:
![alt text](no-such-image.png).

Cited [@ghost2020] with no `bibliography:` declared, so the reference renders as a raw key.

Broken inline math $\frac{$ that KaTeX cannot parse (server-side math-render diagnostic).

A fenced block whose language token is a typo. It renders, just unhighlighted, so only
`validate_code_languages` can tell you the highlighting isn't broken: the label is.

```pyton
x = 1
```

A theorem whose id lacks a cross-reference kind prefix. It is numbered ("Theorem 1")
from its `.theorem` class, but `@pythagoras` can never resolve, so the id is silently
unreferenceable unless the author writes `#thm-pythagoras`.

::: {.theorem #pythagoras}
The square of the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares of the other two sides.
:::
